---
<Layout title="Dhara Gohil — Technical Writer & Knowledge Strategist">
<section class="hero wrap">
<div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> TECHNICAL WRITER & KNOWLEDGE STRATEGIST</p><h1>I turn complexity<br />into <span>clarity.</span><svg viewBox="0 0 280 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 14 Q130 -1 274 9 M36 19 Q145 6 251 15" /></svg></h1><p class="hero-description">Hi, I’m Dhara. I connect people and technology through clear documentation, thoughtful knowledge systems, and a little curiosity.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="#work">Explore my work <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#about">A little about me <span>↓</span></a></div><div class="hero-note"><span class="tiny-line"></span> Developer roots. Writer’s perspective. Human-first thinking.</div></div>
<div class="hero-art" aria-label="Illustration of transforming complex information into clear documentation" role="img"><span class="art-caption">A LITTLE STRUCTURE GOES A LONG WAY.</span><div class="orbit orbit-one"></div><div class="orbit orbit-two"></div><div class="code-note"><span>the complex stuff</span><p><b>{'{'}</b><br />&nbsp; systems: [ideas, data],<br />&nbsp; questions: "how?",<br />&nbsp; possibilities: ∞<br /><b>{'}'}</b></p></div><div class="paper"><div class="paper-top"><span class="mini-logo">d.</span><span>MADE TO MAKE SENSE</span></div><div class="paper-heading">Clarity, by design.</div><div class="paper-line long"></div><div class="paper-line"></div><div class="paper-line medium"></div><div class="paper-rule"></div><div class="paper-item"><i>✓</i><span>Find what you need</span></div><div class="paper-item"><i>✓</i><span>Understand how it works</span></div><div class="paper-item"><i>✓</i><span>Move forward with confidence</span></div><div class="paper-bottom">COMPLEX → CLEAR <span>↗</span></div></div><span class="floating-star">✳</span><span class="hand-note">less friction,<br />more understanding.<svg viewBox="0 0 80 45"><path d="M70 4 Q66 42 8 29 M8 29 L22 22 M8 29 L20 39" /></svg></span></div>
</section>
<div class="credentials"><div class="wrap"><span>14+ years across technology & communication</span><i>✳</i><span>Developer turned technical writer</span><i>✳</i><span>Clarity is always the goal</span></div></div>
<section class="work wrap" id="work"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">A SELECTION OF WHAT I DO</p><h2>Words that do the work<span>.</span></h2></div><p>Different challenges. One common thread.<br />Helping people make sense of the complex.</p></div><div class="filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter projects"><button class="active" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All work <span>04</span></button><button data-filter="technical" aria-pressed="false">Technical writing</button><button data-filter="strategy" aria-pressed="false">Docs-as-code</button><button data-filter="knowledge" aria-pressed="false">Knowledge management</button><button data-filter="ai" aria-pressed="false">AI & documentation</button></div>
<div class="project-grid">{projects.map(p=><a class="project" href={p.href} data-category={p.category}><div class:list={['project-art',p.art]}><span class="project-number">{p.n} / SELECTED WORK</span>{p.art==='docs'?<div class="mini-browser"><div class="browser-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>omnilib / docs</span></div><div class="browser-content"><div class="browser-sidebar">◈ OmniLib<br /><b>Getting started</b><span>Architecture</span><span>API reference</span><span>User guides</span></div><div class="browser-document"><span>THE OMNILIB DOCUMENTATION</span><h4>Everything you need.<br />Clearly documented.</h4><div></div><div></div><code><b>GET</b> /api/v1/books</code></div></div></div>:p.art==='flow'?<div class="flow-diagram"><div>01 <b>Write</b><small>Markdown</small></div><span>→</span><div>02 <b>Review</b><small>Pull request</small></div><span>→</span><div>03 <b>Publish</b><small>Clear docs ↗</small></div><p>GOOD PROCESS. BETTER DOCUMENTATION.</p></div>:p.art==='knowledge'?<div class="knowledge-map"><div class="map-root">Knowledge, connected.</div><div class="map-branches"><span>People</span><span>Processes</span><span>Products</span></div><p>Findable by design.</p></div>:<div class="ai-visual"><div>Human<br /><b>context + judgment</b></div><span>+</span><div>AI<br /><b>exploration + possibility</b></div><p>Thoughtful inputs. Useful outcomes.</p></div>}<div class="art-footer">{p.label}<span>↗</span></div></div><div class="project-meta"><span>{p.type}</span><span>↗</span></div><h3>{p.title}</h3><p>{p.description}</p><div class="tags">{p.tags.map(t=><span>{t}</span>)}</div></a>)}</div>
<div class="case-link"><span>Behind the documentation: the decisions, the process, the lessons.</span><a href="/work/case-studies/documentation-modernization">Explore a case study ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="about-section" id="about"><div class="wrap about"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE PERSON BEHIND THE WORDS</p><h2>A technical mind.<br />A writer’s eye.<br /><span>A human approach.</span></h2></div><div class="about-copy"><p>I started in software development. Today, I help people understand the technology we build.</p><p>With 14+ years across technology and communication, including 9+ years in technical writing, I bring an engineer’s curiosity and a writer’s care to every project.</p><p>My work spans enterprise software, telecommunications, e-commerce, and industrial automation. Whether it’s an API reference or an entire knowledge ecosystem, I believe good documentation starts with understanding the person who needs it.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/dhara-gohil-5630a254" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">More about my journey on LinkedIn ↗</a></div></div></section>
<section class="expertise wrap" id="expertise"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">MY EVERYDAY TOOLKIT</p><h2>Structure meets craft<span>.</span></h2></div><p>The skills and tools behind<br />clear, useful content.</p></div><div class="expertise-list"><div><span>01</span><h3>Technical communication</h3><p>API references · User guides · Architecture documentation · Release notes</p></div><div><span>02</span><h3>Content & knowledge strategy</h3><p>Information architecture · Taxonomy · Content governance · Documentation strategy</p></div><div><span>03</span><h3>Tools & technologies</h3><p>DITA XML · Markdown · Git · Confluence · Oxygen XML · Visual Studio Code</p></div><div><span>04</span><h3>AI & modern workflows</h3><p>AI-assisted authoring · Prompt engineering · Agentic review · Docs-as-code</p></div></div></section>
<section class="contact wrap" id="contact"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> OPEN TO THE NEXT CHAPTER</p><h2>Have something complex?<br />Let’s make it <em>clear.</em></h2><div><p>Let’s talk technical writing, knowledge strategy,<br />or your next documentation challenge.</p><a class="button" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/dhara-gohil-5630a254" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Connect on LinkedIn ↗</a></div><span class="contact-star" aria-hidden="true">✳</span></section>
</Layout>
<script>
const buttons = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-filter]');
buttons.forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
buttons.forEach(item => { item.classList.toggle('active', item === button); item.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(item === button)); });
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-category]').forEach(project => { project.hidden = button.dataset.filter !== 'all' && project.dataset.category !== button.dataset.filter; });
}));
</script>
